    "requirement": "Requirements\n     Internal auditors must understand their information-protection responsibilities and respect\n         the confidentiality, privacy, and ownership of information acquired through audit services\n         or professional relationships.\n     Internal auditors must understand and comply with applicable confidentiality, privacy,\n         and information-security laws, regulations, policies, and procedures.\n     Relevant responsibilities include custody, retention, and disposal of engagement records;\n         release of records to internal and external parties; and handling information, copies, and\n         access when no longer needed.\n     Confidential information must not be disclosed to unauthorized parties unless a legal or\n         professional responsibility requires disclosure.\n     Internal auditors must manage the risk of accidental exposure or disclosure.\n     The chief audit executive must ensure that the internal audit function and individuals\n         assisting it follow the same information-protection requirements.",
