    "summary": " Provide the board and senior management with the information needed to establish the internal audit mandate.",
    "requirement": "Requirements — Chief Audit Executive\n     Provide the board and senior management with the information needed to establish the\n         internal audit mandate.\n     Where laws or regulations prescribe all or part of the mandate, include the applicable\n         legal requirements in the internal audit charter.\n     Coordinate with other internal and external assurance providers to understand their\n         respective roles and responsibilities and help determine the scope and types of internal\n         audit services.\n     Document or reference the mandate in the board-approved internal audit charter.\n     Periodically assess whether changed circumstances justify discussions about the mandate.\n     When warranted, discuss whether the function’s authority, role, and responsibilities\n         remain sufficient to achieve its strategy and objectives.\nEssential Conditions — Board\n     Discuss the appropriate authority, role, and responsibilities of internal audit with the chief\n         audit executive and senior management.\n     Approve the internal audit charter, including the mandate and the scope and types of\n         services.\nEssential Conditions — Senior Management\n     Participate in mandate discussions and communicate expectations for the board’s\n         consideration.\n     Support the mandate throughout the organization and promote the authority granted to\n         internal audit.",
