    "requirement": "Requirements — Chief Audit Executive\nDevelop and maintain an internal audit charter covering, at a minimum:\n     The Purpose of Internal Auditing.\n     Commitment to the Global Internal Audit Standards.\n     The mandate, including the scope and types of services.\n     The board’s responsibilities and expectations regarding management’s support for\n         internal audit.\n     Organizational positioning and reporting relationships.\nDiscuss the proposed charter with the board and senior management to confirm that it accurately\nreflects their understanding and expectations.\nEssential Conditions — Board\n     Discuss additional charter provisions needed to enable an effective internal audit\n         function.\n     Approve the charter.\n     Review the charter with the chief audit executive in light of organizational changes,\n         including changes in audit leadership and the nature, severity, or interrelationships of\n         risks.\nEssential Conditions — Senior Management\n     Communicate expectations that should be considered for inclusion in the charter.",
