      "Considerations for Implementation\nExpected competencies should reflect the internal audit mandate, organizational complexity,\nspecific needs, risk profile, industry, and jurisdiction.\nA job description typically documents desired qualifications and competencies, which may\ninclude:\n     Comprehensive knowledge of the Global Internal Audit Standards and leading internal\n         audit practices.\n     Experience establishing and managing an effective internal audit function.\n     Experience recruiting, training, and developing internal auditors.\n     A Certified Internal Auditor designation or other relevant professional education,\n         certifications, and credentials.\n     Leadership experience.\n     Industry or sector experience.\nThese are examples of desired qualifications. The standard does not prescribe the CIA\ndesignation as a universal requirement.\nA CAE may bring other relevant expertise, supplemented by the competencies of the internal\naudit team. Where the CAE enters from another role or sector, collaboration with experienced\ncolleagues and professional networking can support development.\nThe board should encourage continuing professional education and other development\nopportunities.\nSuccession planning should identify potential internal or external replacements, align with the\norganization’s broader succession arrangements, and be shared with the board and senior\nmanagement."
