    "summary": "The CAE must evaluate whether internal audit has sufficient resources to fulfill its mandate and achieve its plan. When resources are insufficient, the CAE must:  Develop a strategy to obtain sufficient resources.",
    "requirement": "Requirements — Chief Audit Executive\nThe CAE must evaluate whether internal audit has sufficient resources to fulfill its mandate and\nachieve its plan.\nWhen resources are insufficient, the CAE must:\n     Develop a strategy to obtain sufficient resources.\n     Inform the board about the impact of the shortfall.\n     Explain how the shortfall will be addressed.\nThe assessment should consider the resources needed to deliver the work effectively, including\nrelevant capabilities.\nEssential Conditions — Board\nThe board should:\n     Work with senior management to provide sufficient resources.\n     Discuss resource sufficiency with the CAE at least annually, considering both resource\n         numbers and capabilities.\n     Consider the effect of insufficient resources on internal audit’s mandate and plan.\n     Work with senior management and the CAE to address resource deficiencies.\nEssential Conditions — Senior Management\nSenior management should work with the board to provide sufficient resources and collaborate\nwith the CAE to address shortages.",
    "implementation": [
      "Considerations for Implementation\nA resource assessment can compare required resources against available capacity, skills, funding,\nand technology.\nThe resulting strategy may include:\n     Additional budget or staffing.\n     Specialist expertise.\n     Outsourcing or co-sourcing.\n     Guest auditors.\n     Training and development.\n     Technology that improves audit effectiveness and efficiency.\nAnnual resource discussions often take place alongside approval of the internal audit plan. More\nfrequent discussions may be useful when risks, staffing, or planned activities change. Quarterly\ndiscussion is a leading practice rather than a mandatory frequency in this standard."
    ],
    "conformance": [
      "Examples of Evidence of Conformance\n     Documented resource assessments and gap analyses.\n     Staffing and resource plans.\n     Budget submissions.\n     Cost-benefit analyses of resourcing options.\n     Board minutes discussing resource sufficiency.\n     Communications explaining shortages, consequences, and proposed responses."
    ],
