    "requirement": "Requirements — Chief Audit Executive\nThe CAE must develop, implement, and maintain a quality assurance and improvement\nprogram (QAIP) covering all aspects of the internal audit function.\nThe program must include:\n     Internal quality assessments.\n     External quality assessments.\nThe CAE must communicate:\n     Internal quality assessment results to the board and senior management at least annually.\n     External quality assessment results when completed.\nThese communications must address:\n     Conformance with the Global Internal Audit Standards.\n     Achievement of internal audit performance objectives.\n     Compliance with laws and regulations relevant to the internal audit function, where\n         applicable.\n     Plans to address deficiencies and improvement opportunities, where applicable.\nEssential Conditions — Board\nThe board should:\n     Discuss the QAIP with the CAE.\n     Approve internal audit performance objectives at least annually.\n     Assess the function’s effectiveness and efficiency.\n     Consider conformance with the Standards and relevant laws and regulations.\n     Consider mandate fulfillment and completion of the audit plan.\n     Review QAIP results and determine whether performance objectives have been achieved.\nEssential Conditions — Senior Management\nSenior management should:\n     Provide input into internal audit performance objectives.\n     Participate with the board in the annual assessment of the CAE and internal audit\n         function.",
