      "Considerations for Implementation\nThe CAE should follow the organization’s budgeting processes. An adequate internal audit\nbudget should receive board approval whether the function is internally staffed or outsourced.\nBudget monitoring should compare planned and actual expenditure and analyze significant\nvariances to determine whether adjustments are needed.\nA budget may include reserves for unexpected but necessary changes to the audit plan. This is an\nimplementation option, not a requirement to maintain a particular reserve amount.\nWhere internal audit funding forms part of another department’s or authority’s budget, the CAE\nshould still:\n     Understand the amount allocated to internal audit.\n     Track internal audit expenditure.\n     Monitor whether available funding remains sufficient.\nSignificant additional funding needs arising from unforeseen circumstances should be discussed\npromptly with the board and senior management."
