    "sourcePdf": "assets/standards/standard-11.pdf",
    "summary": "The CAE must communicate internal audit results to the board and senior management periodically and for individual engagements as appropriate.",
    "requirement": "Requirements\nThe CAE must communicate internal audit results to the board and senior management\nperiodically and for individual engagements as appropriate. The CAE must understand their\nexpectations regarding the nature and timing of these communications.\nResults can include:\n     Individual engagement conclusions.\n     Themes across engagements, including effective practices and common root causes.\n     Conclusions about a business unit or the organization overall.\nA. Engagement conclusions\nThe CAE must:\n     Review and approve final engagement communications, including their conclusions.\n     Determine recipients and distribution methods before release.\n     Retain overall responsibility when review, approval, or distribution duties are delegated.\n     Seek advice from legal counsel and/or senior management, as required, before external\n         release, subject to applicable legal or regulatory requirements and restrictions.\nB. Themes across engagements\nWhen the CAE identifies themes concerning governance, risk management, or control processes,\nthese must be communicated to the board and senior management in a timely manner, together\nwith relevant insights, advice, and/or conclusions.\nC. Business-unit or organization-level conclusions\nWhere such a conclusion is required, it must be supported by relevant, reliable, and sufficient\ninformation.\nCommunication of the conclusion must include:\n    1. A summary of the request.\n    2. The criteria used to reach the conclusion.\n    3. The scope, limitations, and period covered.\n    4. A summary of supporting information.\n    5. Disclosure of reliance on other assurance providers, where applicable.",
