    "requirement": "Requirements\nInternal auditors must gather information that meets three characteristics:\nCharacteristic                              Meaning\nRelevant        Supports the engagement objectives, falls within its scope, and contributes to\n                the results.\nCharacteristic           Meaning\nReliable        Is factual and current. Reliability is strengthened through direct collection,\n                independent sources, corroboration, and effective controls over the source\n                system.\nSufficient      Provides an adequate basis for analysis and evaluation and enables an informed,\n                competent person to repeat the work and reach the same conclusions.\nInternal auditors must:\n Evaluate the relevance, reliability, and sufficiency of the information used to support\n    potential findings and conclusions.\n Apply professional skepticism when assessing information reliability.\n Determine whether additional information is needed when the available evidence does\n    not adequately support the engagement findings.\n Determine whether the inability to obtain relevant evidence should itself be identified as\n    a finding.",
