    "practicalApplication": "Practical Application\nThe following fields can support a future action-monitoring function or be presented as a\npractical reference within the standard.\n                   Field                                        Purpose\nEngagement reference               Links the action to the relevant engagement.\nFinding reference and title        Identifies the issue being addressed.\nFinding significance               Supports prioritization and follow-up planning.\nRecommendation or agreed action    Records the response to the finding.\nResponsible individual             Identifies management accountability.\nOriginal completion date           Preserves the initial commitment.\n                                   Records an approved or accepted change, where\nRevised completion date            applicable.\n                                   Explains changes in implementation timing.\nReason for delay or revision       Records management’s progress statement.\nManagement-reported status         Links to evidence of implementation.\nSupporting evidence                Records the procedures performed and their results.\nInternal audit verification        Distinguishes verified status from management’s\n                                   assertion.\nInternal audit-confirmed status    Records changes to the proposed response and their\n                                   assessment.\nAlternative action details         Documents matters requiring chief audit executive\n                                   consideration.\nEscalation or risk-acceptance      Shows the currency of the record.\nassessment\nLast update and confirmation date\nSuggested Status Labels\nThese labels are practical design options rather than prescribed IIA terminology.\n                Status                                            Meaning\nNot Started\nIn Progress                        Management has not begun implementation.\nManagement Reports Complete\n— Verification Pending             Implementation is underway.\nVerified Complete                  Management has reported completion; internal audit\n                                   confirmation is pending.\nPartially Implemented\n                                   Internal audit has confirmed implementation through\n                                   procedures appropriate to the finding’s significance.\n                                   Some elements are complete, but the action is not fully\n                                   implemented.\nStatus  Meaning\nAlternative Action Under Review A revised response is being evaluated.\nOverdue should be a separate indicator based on the completion date, so an action can remain\nboth “In Progress” and “Overdue.” Any recorded risk acceptance should include the supporting\ndecision and escalation assessment; it should not be treated as proof that the action was\nimplemented."
